sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To cut a given uncut straight line similarly to a given cut straight line.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be the given uncut straight line, and {AC} the straight line cut at the points {D} and {E}, and let them be so placed as to contain any angle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="340" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.10 diagram" src="propVI10.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // CB is joined, DF and EG drawn parallel to it and DHK parallel to AB
    // (I.31); FH and HB are parallelograms (I.34), and VI.2 twice with V.7
    // carries the cuts at D and E over to F and G.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the triangle ABC (random face), DF, EG and DK;
    // F' and G' are his hidden parallelogram helpers. The given lines AB and
    // AC stand alone until "Join CB", so they and CB are solid twins (ABs,
    // ACs, CBs) hidden at rest (initiallyHidden); the filled triangle joins
    // the slides once CB is drawn. DF, EG and DK are declared from D, E and
    // D, so they stroke as drawn. The proof also names AB, AC, CB, the
    // segments AD, DE, EC, AF, FG, GB, DH, HK, EH, CK, the parallelograms FH
    // (FGHD) and HB (HGBK) and the triangles DCK and AEG: all transparent
    // (;0;0;0 lines, ;0;0;0;0 polygons), so the resting figure is unchanged.
    // Prose and caption refs go to these transparent targets, never to the
    // filled triangle, which is not highlighted (#140). One marker for "any
    // angle" at A (not a right angle); markers are hidden at rest.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C (free) and D, E
    // (lineSlider on AC), all givens on slide 1. F', F, G', G, K, H are
    // derived and listed from the slide that draws them.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","E","ABs","ACs","AB","AC","AD","DE","EC"];
    var ANG   = GIVEN.concat(["angA"]);
    var PAR1  = ANG.concat(["CBs","CB","DF","F","EG","G","AF","FG","GB"]);
    var PAR2  = PAR1.concat(["ABC","DK","H","K","DH","HK","EH","CK",
                             "FH","HB","DCK","AEG"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.10",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;30,270",
            "B;point;free;250,270",
            "C;point;free;290,30",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A,C,90,200",
            "E;point;lineSlider;A,C,150,80",
            "F';point;parallelogram;B,C,D;0;0",
            "F;point;intersection;A,B,D,F'",
            "DF;line;connect;D,F",
            "G';point;parallelogram;B,C,E;0;0",
            "G;point;intersection;A,B,E,G'",
            "EG;line;connect;E,G",
            "K;point;parallelogram;D,F,B",
            "DK;line;connect;D,K",
            "H;point;intersection;D,K,E,G",
            // Slide twins of the given lines and the join, hidden at rest.
            "ABs;line;connect;A,B",
            "ACs;line;connect;A,C",
            "CBs;line;connect;C,B",
            // Lines and segments, as transparent highlight targets.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;0",
            "CB;line;connect;C,B;0;0;0",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D;0;0;0",
            "DE;line;connect;D,E;0;0;0",
            "EC;line;connect;E,C;0;0;0",
            "AF;line;connect;A,F;0;0;0",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G;0;0;0",
            "GB;line;connect;G,B;0;0;0",
            "DH;line;connect;D,H;0;0;0",
            "HK;line;connect;H,K;0;0;0",
            "EH;line;connect;E,H;0;0;0",
            "CK;line;connect;C,K;0;0;0",
            // The parallelograms and triangles of the argument. Explicit ;0 faces.
            "FH;polygon;quadrilateral;F,G,H,D;0;0;0;0",
            "HB;polygon;quadrilateral;H,G,B,K;0;0;0;0",
            "DCK;polygon;triangle;D,C,K;0;0;0;0",
            "AEG;polygon;triangle;A,E,G;0;0;0;0",
            "angA;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["ABs","ACs","CBs"],
        aliases: { "DHK": "DK", "BA": "AB", "CA": "AC", "BC": "CB", "GF": "FG",
                   "BG": "GB", "HD": "DH", "KH": "HK", "HE": "EH", "KC": "CK",
                   "ED": "DE", "CE": "EC", "DA": "AD", "FA": "AF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To cut a given uncut straight line similarly to a given cut straight line.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","D","E"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.10" }] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be the given uncut straight line,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "and {AC} the straight line cut at the points {D} and {E},",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","D","E"] },
            { text: "and let them be so placed as to contain any angle.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","angA"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Join {CB}, and draw {DF} and {EG} through {D} and {E} parallel to {CB},",
              visible: PAR1,
              highlighted: ["CB","DF","EG"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "CBs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DF",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "F",   name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "EG",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "G",   name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" },
                               { claim: "DF and EG parallel to CB", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "and draw {DHK|DK} through {D} parallel to {AB}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DK","AB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "DK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "H",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "K",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "DHK parallel to AB", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the figures {FH} and {HB} is a parallelogram.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["FH","HB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "FH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "HB", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore {DH} equals {FG} and {HK} equals {GB}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DH","FG","HK","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal", ref: "I.34" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the straight line {EH} is parallel to a side {CK} of the triangle {DCK},",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["EH","CK","DCK"] },
            { text: "therefore, proportionally, {DE} is to {EC} as {DH} is to {HK}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DE","EC","DH","HK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a parallel to a side cuts the sides proportionally", ref: "VI.2" }] },
            { text: "But {DH} equals {FG}, and {HK} equals {GB},",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DH","FG","HK","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DE","EC","FG","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals have the same ratio to the same", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "Again, since {DF} is parallel to a side {EG} of the triangle {AEG},",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DF","EG","AEG"] },
            { text: "therefore, proportionally, {AD} is to {DE} as {AF} is to {FG}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["AD","DE","AF","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a parallel to a side cuts the sides proportionally", ref: "VI.2" }] },
            { text: "But it was also proved that {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB},",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DE","EC","FG","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB},",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["DE","EC","FG","GB"] },
            { text: "and {AD} is to {DE} as {AF} is to {FG}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["AD","DE","AF","FG"] },
            { text: "Therefore the given uncut straight line {AB} has been cut similarly to the given cut straight line {AC}.",
              visible: PAR2,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG","GB","AD","DE","EC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.10") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.31":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "I.34":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI34/",
        "V.7":      "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "VI.2":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI2/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Join {CB}, and draw {DF} and {EG} through {D} and {E} parallel to {CB}, and draw {DHK} through {D} parallel to {AB}. [!just I.31]

Therefore each of the figures {FH} and {HB} is a parallelogram. Therefore {DH} equals {FG} and {HK} equals {GB}. [!just I.34]

Now, since the straight line {EH} is parallel to a side {CK} of the triangle {DCK}, therefore, proportionally, {DE} is to {EC} as {DH} is to {HK}. [!just VI.2]

But {DH} equals {FG}, and {HK} equals {GB}, therefore {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB}. [!just V.7]

Again, since {DF} is parallel to a side {EG} of the triangle {AEG}, therefore, proportionally, {AD} is to {DE} as {AF} is to {FG}. [!just VI.2]

But it was also proved that {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB}, therefore {DE} is to {EC} as {FG} is to {GB}, and {AD} is to {DE} as {AF} is to {FG}.

Therefore the given uncut straight line {AB} has been cut similarly to the given cut straight line {AC}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

In a sense, this proposition is a generalization of the last one @VI.9. Prop. VI.9 cut a line into two parts whose ratio was a given numerical ratio. This proposition cuts a line into two parts whose ratio is a given ratio of two other lines. Both propositions rely on @VI.2 as a basis to make any conclusion about the ratio of two lines.

#### Use of this construction

This proposition is not used later in the *Elements,* but it is a basic construction of geometry.
